#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RHEL-Install-RPMs.rst:48
msgid "Set locale"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/_RHEL-Set-Locale.rst:1
msgid ""
"Make sure you have a locale which supports ``UTF-8``. If you are in a "
"minimal environment (such as a docker container), the locale may be "
"something minimal like ``C``. We test with the following settings. However, "
"it should be fine if you're using a different UTF-8 supported locale."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/_RHEL-Set-Locale.rst:6
msgid ""
"$ locale  # check for UTF-8\n"
"\n"
"$ sudo dnf install langpacks-en glibc-langpack-en\n"
"$ export LANG=en_US.UTF-8\n"
"\n"
"$ locale  # verify settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RHEL-Install-RPMs.rst:53
msgid "Enable required repositories"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RHEL-Install-RPMs.rst:57
msgid "RHEL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RHEL-Install-RPMs.rst:59
msgid ""
"You will need to enable the EPEL repositories and the CodeReady Builder "
"(CRB) repository:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RHEL-Install-RPMs.rst:61
msgid ""
"$ sudo dnf install -y https://dl.fedoraproject.org/pub/epel/epel-release-"
"latest-$(rpm -E %rhel).noarch.rpm\n"
"$ sudo env FORCE_DNF=1 crb enable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RHEL-Install-RPMs.rst:66
msgid ""
"This step may be slightly different depending on the distribution you are "
"using. `Check the EPEL documentation <https://docs.fedoraproject.org/en-US/"
"epel/getting-started/>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RHEL-Install-RPMs.rst:69
msgid "Next, download the ``ros2-release`` package and install it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RHEL-Install-RPMs.rst:71
msgid ""
"$ sudo dnf install curl\n"
"$ export ROS_APT_SOURCE_VERSION=$(curl -s https://api.github.com/repos/ros-"
"infrastructure/ros-apt-source/releases/latest | grep -F \"tag_name\" | awk "
"-F'\"' '{print $4}')\n"
"$ sudo dnf install \"https://github.com/ros-infrastructure/ros-apt-source/"
"releases/download/${ROS_APT_SOURCE_VERSION}/ros2-release-$"
"{ROS_APT_SOURCE_VERSION}-1.el.noarch.rpm\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RHEL-Install-RPMs.rst:77
msgid "Fedora"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RHEL-Install-RPMs.rst:79
msgid "Download the ``ros2-release`` package and install it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RHEL-Install-RPMs.rst:81
msgid ""
"$ sudo dnf install curl\n"
"$ export ROS_APT_SOURCE_VERSION=$(curl -s https://api.github.com/repos/ros-"
"infrastructure/ros-apt-source/releases/latest | grep -F \"tag_name\" | awk "
"-F'\"' '{print $4}')\n"
"$ sudo dnf install \"https://github.com/ros-infrastructure/ros-apt-source/"
"releases/download/${ROS_APT_SOURCE_VERSION}/ros2-release-$"
"{ROS_APT_SOURCE_VERSION}-1.fc.noarch.rpm\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RHEL-Install-RPMs.rst:87
msgid ""
"The `ros2-release <https://github.com/ros-infrastructure/ros-apt-source/>`_ "
"package provides keys and repo configuration for the various ROS "
"repositories. Updates to repository configuration will occur automatically "
"when new versions of this package are released to the ROS repositories."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RHEL-Install-RPMs.rst:91
msgid "Install development tools (optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RHEL-Install-RPMs.rst:93
msgid ""
"If you are going to build ROS packages or otherwise do development, you can "
"also install the development tools:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RHEL-Install-RPMs.rst:95
msgid ""
"$ sudo dnf install -y \\\n"
"  cmake \\\n"
"  gcc-c++ \\\n"
"  git \\\n"
"  make \\\n"
"  patch \\\n"
"  python3-colcon-common-extensions \\\n"
"  python3-mypy \\\n"
"  python3-pip \\\n"
"  python3-pytest \\\n"
"  python3-pytest-repeat \\\n"
"  python3-pytest-rerunfailures \\\n"
"  python3-rosdep \\\n"
"  python3-setuptools \\\n"
"  python3-vcstool \\\n"
"  wget"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RHEL-Install-RPMs.rst:115
msgid "Install ROS 2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/_Dnf-Update-Admonition.rst:1
msgid ""
"ROS 2 packages are built on frequently updated RHEL systems. It is always "
"recommended that you ensure your system is up to date before installing new "
"packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/_Dnf-Update-Admonition.rst:4
msgid "$ sudo dnf update"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RHEL-Install-RPMs.rst:119
msgid "Desktop Install (Recommended): ROS, RViz, demos, tutorials."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RHEL-Install-RPMs.rst:121
msgid "$ sudo dnf install ros-rolling-desktop"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RHEL-Install-RPMs.rst:125
msgid ""
"ROS-Base Install (Bare Bones): Communication libraries, message packages, "
"command line tools. No GUI tools."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RHEL-Install-RPMs.rst:128
msgid "$ sudo dnf install ros-rolling-ros-base"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RHEL-Install-RPMs.rst:133
msgid "Install additional RMW implementations (optional)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RHEL-Install-RPMs.rst:135
msgid ""
"The default middleware that ROS 2 uses is ``Fast DDS``, but the middleware "
"(RMW) can be replaced at runtime. See the :doc:`guide <RMW-Implementations/"
"Working-with-multiple-RMW-implementations>` on how to work with multiple "
"RMWs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RHEL-Install-RPMs.rst:139
msgid "Setup environment"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RHEL-Install-RPMs.rst:141
msgid "Set up your environment by sourcing the following file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RHEL-Install-RPMs.rst:143
msgid "$ source /opt/ros/rolling/setup.bash"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RHEL-Install-RPMs.rst:149
msgid ""
"Replace ``.bash`` with your shell if you're not using console. Possible "
"values are: ``setup.bash``, ``setup.sh``, ``setup.zsh``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RHEL-Install-RPMs.rst:153
msgid "Try some examples"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RHEL-Install-RPMs.rst:155
msgid ""
"If you installed ``ros-rolling-desktop`` above you can try some examples."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RHEL-Install-RPMs.rst:157
msgid ""
"In one terminal, source the setup file and then run a C++ ``talker``\\ :"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RHEL-Install-RPMs.rst:159
msgid ""
"$ source /opt/ros/rolling/setup.bash\n"
"$ ros2 run demo_nodes_cpp talker"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RHEL-Install-RPMs.rst:164
msgid ""
"In another terminal source the setup file and then run a Python "
"``listener``\\ :"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RHEL-Install-RPMs.rst:166
msgid ""
"$ source /opt/ros/rolling/setup.bash\n"
"$ ros2 run demo_nodes_py listener"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RHEL-Install-RPMs.rst:171
msgid ""
"You should see the ``talker`` saying that it's ``Publishing`` messages and "
"the ``listener`` saying ``I heard`` those messages. This verifies both the C+"
"+ and Python APIs are working properly. Hooray!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Installation/RHEL-Install-RPMs.rst:175
msgid ""
"If you want to use other RMW implementations, you can check the :doc:`guide "
"<RMW-Implementations>`."
msgstr ""

